        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-01T19:00:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "can we instead set a global variable so that all RST and RBOX handlers check that variable first and re-assert EC reset and keep it there? or maybe just do it inside deassert_ec_rst() and turn it into NOP if this variable is set. \n\nthis way we leave a way to get EC out of reset through a debug console w/o powercycle (would need a new command for it, which maybe CR50_DEV or widely enabled) w/o this deferred call reasserting it back again every 100ms. useful for dev machines.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 78,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "de207f5014a1dd8c128956142bc541362208a973",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c409ea50_c948e147",
        "filename": "board/cr50/power_button.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-02T01:24:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I did not feel comfortable using a gobal variable to control EC reset functions - because the functions are in a different source file, and because conceivably EC reset could be deasserted without calling the function, but by just writing into the Rbox register.\n\nSo I added a local static variable which could be set to keep the system in reset, and added a dev command to report the variable state and to allow to clear the variable if dev image is running.",
      "parentUuid": "fc2162fc_7666a0c7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 78,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "de207f5014a1dd8c128956142bc541362208a973",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d943d0b8_5f1b2782",
        "filename": "board/cr50/power_button.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-02T04:04:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e  because the functions are in a different source file\n\nwe could have set_deassert_allowed_state(bool), which would be implemented and set a variable in board/cr50/board.c, where [de]assert_ec_rst() functions reside. similar to what post_reboot_request() does there.\nor the other way around - how uart_bitbang_is_enabled() is used in [de]assert_ec_rst().\n\n\u003e because conceivably EC reset could be deasserted without calling the function, but by just writing into the Rbox register.\n\nyes, this may be a good reason indeed, if EC reset can be asserted/deasserted as a result of an external signal coming into Rbox and directly affecting EC reset while H1 is in deep sleep, for example. or can AP initiate EC reset bypassing H1?\notherwise: do we ever do it - don\u0027t go to deassert_ec_rst() and just make a direct change in registers? why?",
      "parentUuid": "c409ea50_c948e147",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 78,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "de207f5014a1dd8c128956142bc541362208a973",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cbbc085c_66b15a9a",
        "filename": "board/cr50/power_button.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-02T14:48:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "EC can be reset by writing into RBOX_ASSERT_EC_RST, this happens in two places in the code already, more could be added by some future contributor either for a good reason, or for lack of awareness about this \u0027hold in reset\u0027 requirement. This is why I thought it is better to have an independent function/thread to enforce the state, but I can change this if you feel strongly about it.\n\nEC reset is also pulsed when power+refresh are pressed (even though it is asserted again by the RO and deasserted by rbox_release_ec_reset()).",
      "parentUuid": "d943d0b8_5f1b2782",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 78,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "de207f5014a1dd8c128956142bc541362208a973",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f9c295d0_d2878e6f",
        "filename": "board/cr50/power_button.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-02T19:20:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e if you feel strongly about it\n\njust feels weird to enforce it by periodic reasserting when we are in full control of it. maybe better to centralize all accesses to EC reset? this is not the only place that\u0027ll break if code meddles with registers directly instead of going through proper functions. maybe do it in a followup CL?\n\n\u003e this happens in two places in the code already\n\nI only see it board.c - in ec_rst-specific functions plus ac_stayed_disconnected(). does direct RBOX_ASSERT_EC_RST access happen somewhere else?\n\nif yes, can it break other things that [de]assert_ec_rst() currently ensure - handling uart config for bitbang, holding assert for certain time? maybe another reason to centralize handling EC resets?\n\n\u003e reset is also pulsed when power+refresh are pressed (even though it is asserted again by the RO...)\n\nthose are the cases, which would force us to use periodic reassertion. looks like in this case we are ok, so can still consider going through deassert_ec_rst() everywhere.",
      "parentUuid": "cbbc085c_66b15a9a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 78,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "de207f5014a1dd8c128956142bc541362208a973",
